## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001, 120105
## Title: ZacUI |cff33ff99Raid tools|r
## Notes: The raid helpers ZacUI's boss mods lean on: /pull, /break and /range in every boss mod's language, the raid sync between raiders, and the raid callouts' speech settings.
## Author: Zac
## Version: 3.0.10
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ZacUI\Media\addonIcon
## X-Category: Interface Enhancements
## Dependencies: Zacui
## OptionalDeps: Zacui_Auras, LibSharedMedia-3.0
## X-ZacUI-Part: Raid tools

# Part of ZacUI. It shares ZacUI's namespace (_G.ZacUI, published by
# Core_Boot) and its saved variables; its settings live in ZacUIDB under
# the aura engine's key and travel with that profile section.
#
# Zacui_Auras is an optional dependency so that, when the engine is on,
# it has loaded first: the raid sync uses the engine's own codec and comm
# framing.
#
# No media. The raid callouts are spoken by the game's text-to-speech,
# the alert sounds are the game's own (Zacui\Core\Core_Sounds.lua), and
# the raid mods' shapes are in Zacui_RaidMods\Media\Own.
#
# LibSharedMedia is embedded so ZacUI's fonts and bar textures can be
# looked up by name whatever else is enabled; LibStub keeps the first
# copy loaded, so this is a no-op when another addon already carries it.

Libs\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs\LibSharedMedia-3.0.lua

RaidTools.lua
